WEBVTT

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.060
I can't concentrate.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.550
Pull yourself together!

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.070
At this rate, even causing problems at work is...

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.180
You've got mail.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.370
And I know why this is.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.520
It's because...

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.580
Kou Yukina

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.500
What is this?

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.190
Please come by to look at it.
I'll be waiting for you.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.220
Has he gone crazy?

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.010
I can't go to this thing!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.470
I mean,

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.970
ever since that happened,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.970
I haven't been able to
think about anything else.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.460
Oh, jeez!

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.580
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.580
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.130
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.130
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.760
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.760
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.560
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.560
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.560
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.560
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.400
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.400
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.780
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.780
If I reach out my hand

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.160
hajimete no kimochi

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.160
Will you understand my feelings?

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.540
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.540
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.920
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.920
I love you more and more every second

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.050
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.050
We're still far from a happy ending

00:01:53.170 --> 00:02:02.010
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:01:53.170 --> 00:02:02.010
But I want to make it come true

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.470
tsuzuite yuku

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.470
Our story continues

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.640
Huh?

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.600
I mean...

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.380
You shouldn't joke about that.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.400
Kisa, I...

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:19.940
This is bad!

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.980
I've got a handover now, so...

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.780
See you.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.140
Kisa!

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.960
What was that kiss, anyway?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.230
Damn it!

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.410
Why didn't I just ask him?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.240
If this was like any other time,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.120
I would have just jumped in head-first,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.220
without worrying about any consequences.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.660
To: Kou Yukina
Subject: Re: It's Yukina from Marimo Books
Thank you for your email

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.480
That's right...

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.970
Yukina's my dream guy,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.960
To: Kou Yukina
Subject: Re: It's Yukina from Marimo Books
Thank you for your email
I definitely

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.980
so my usual self would
definitely do just that.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.100
But back then,

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.230
for some reason I couldn't
behave the way I usually do.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.160
But that's all for the best.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.680
I bet he's never even thought about
being with another guy before.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.280
So I didn't embarrass myself by
letting my expectations run wild.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:08.370
And then,

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:13.190
if you look at the way he acts around girls,

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.100
it's clear that there's no way he's serious.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.000
That's right!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.010
No matter how I look at it,
it's obvious he was just playing.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.640
But it's not like I didn't already know that.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.140
I know this. I don't need to
agonize over every little thing.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.020
Kisa, I need those documents.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.060
Huh?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.320
The proposal.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.800
Remember? It's due today.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.320
I'm so very sorry!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.260
It completely slipped my mind!

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.590
I'll write it right away!

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.940
Just have it done by the end of the day.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.400
I will!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:43.860
Shit...

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.780
What the hell am I doing?

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.620
Oh, and can you look these over?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.210
And these?

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.770
Yes, yes, yes!

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.790
I'll do whatever you want.
Just leave it here!

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.300
I guess you'd never make a
mistake like this, huh, Takano?

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.060
You have any secrets for
not forgetting stuff?

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.170
No.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.680
I just do it.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.000
Oh, is that so?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.680
Mr. Takano!

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.810
I've got a request for a second
release of this month's edition.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.790
They said they want 5,000 extra copies...

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.430
...of just Kagawa's book,
and see how it goes from there.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:25.070
Stop being so stingy and make it 10,000.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.320
It's obvious that they'll
run out again right away.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.770
You'll have to tell that
to Mr. Yokozawa yourself.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.460
I guess they only need extra
copies of Takano's book.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.520
Well, his book has a different circulation,

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.860
and a different reader base than mine,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.010
so you can't really compare them.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.290
And then, it's not like my
book sold badly at all.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.180
But when there's such an obvious
discrepancy in the results,

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.850
I can't deny that it stings.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.730
Takano's younger than me, too.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.230
Not that age really matters in this job.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.810
I guess it's a combination of small things.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.610
First, he hardly ever makes mistakes.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.200
Even if he did,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.880
he's probably skilled
enough to fix everything.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.210
They're just little things,

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:19.630
but maybe all of them added up
really make all the difference.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.790
I do think my book is really good.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.600
But it's not enough that I think it's good.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.640
It needs to sell.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.260
It's possible that this book
could have sold more copies,

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.400
if someone else was editing it.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.020
What am I saying?

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.560
This is bad.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.400
I'm getting too negative.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.280
Come on,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.030
just finish writing that proposal
before drowning in self-pity!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.910
Oh, yeah. I've got to write Yukina back.

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:57.350
Well, I guess I don't have to.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.420
No, I should at least say thanks.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.920
Come on, just concentrate!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.590
At least I've gotten the proposal done.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.160
Would you like to save the changes to Document 1?
Yes(Y) No(N) Cancel

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.680
Oh, no!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.060
This is so depressing.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.250
And next thing I know, I've come here.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.940
But they're doing a promotion,

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.550
so I should check in at least once.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.650
See if anything's wrong...

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.040
I don't want to run into him though,

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.920
so I'll just do a quick
check and then go home.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.290
Good.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.760
It looks like he's not here.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:48.870
Oh, it's you, Kisa!

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.960
Good evening!

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.690
I sent you an email not long ago.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:54.910
Did you read it?

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.270
Oh, well...

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.270
It's quite the work of art,

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.270
so you should see it in person.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.430
Did you come here after work?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:05.650
Sure...

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.710
What the hell is he doing?

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.190
Is he trying to act like everything's normal?

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.430
Or did it really mean
absolutely nothing to him?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.240
I bet...

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.480
...it's the latter.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.460
I think...it's a little over the top.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.940
Oh. Really?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.670
Here I was thinking that
it still needed something more.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.310
Oh, we're just on time.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.000
This happens hourly.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:41.750
Staff Recommendation

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.160
It's nine o'clock!

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.490
It's nine o'clock!

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.080
I don't know...

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.340
What's wrong with it?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.560
This is great!
This is so cute!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.610
See, there are customers
who love Tinkle.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.990
And it's selling your books.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.880
Uh, no...

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.300
I don't find anything wrong with it.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.550
If anything, I kind of feel bad that you...

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.810
...spent so much time making
this impressive display.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.630
Oh, it was nothing.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.040
I made it for the person
creating my favorite book,

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.630
so I just got all enthusiastic.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.890
Have you been really busy lately?

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.780
You haven't been coming here.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:20.140
Yeah. My work has piled up a bit.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.920
Then I guess I'll go now.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.270
Thanks for the display.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:25.650
Kisa!

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:29.690
Wh-?

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.610
What?

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.780
My shift here is almost over.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.620
Could I have some of your time?

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:39.660
Wh-What for?

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.270
I wanted to talk about...

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.330
...what happened the other day.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.710
Yukina!

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.710
Just wait for me at that café.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:55.640
Huh?

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:56.840
Wait!

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.160
Hello!

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.660
On the way home after work?

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:00.390
Yeah.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.930
Hey, do you want to go get something
to eat when you're done?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.170
Hmm, well...

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.810
I guess I could go if I sell
another twenty volumes.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.860
Are you trying to make
me buy out the store?

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:16.650
The girls love him.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.520
What does he want to talk about?

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:24.320
Realistically, he's probably...

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.960
...going to try to apologize
for the kiss or make excuses.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.230
Our ages are too far apart...

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.960
We're both guys,

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.340
and he can get any girl he wants.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.940
Relationships in real life...

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:40.730
...simply don't work the
way they do in manga.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.290
What the hell am I doing?

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:46.980
Hey.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.860
I'm not breaking up with you.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.880
It's fine, we weren't even going out.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:56.860
How can you say that?

00:09:57.310 --> 00:10:00.660
We said that our thing
was no strings attached,

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.640
from the very start.

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:06.470
If I did something to
lead you on, I'm sorry.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.440
But seriously, it's just
not going to work out.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.500
Why not?!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.340
Did you feel nothing for me?

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.280
I told you, I only liked your looks!

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.570
I don't fall for anyone,

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.980
so stop pushing all these
expectations on me!

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.810
So what,

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:26.170
now you've fallen for that sales boy's face?

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.070
You've been going to his store every day.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.540
So, have you two done it yet?

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.650
Of course not!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.400
What's that all about?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.780
Well, he's obviously straight.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:43.140
Then maybe I'll go tell him.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:43.740
What?

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.790
Stop!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.080
This doesn't have anything
to do with you!

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.290
Shouta, you never fall in
love with anyone, right?

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.670
So just do it with him
and get it over with.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.920
No. He's...

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.790
Yukina is...

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.180
What, you don't want him to find out?

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:05.930
Of course I don't!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.180
Then you should listen to me and...

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:14.690
Whoa.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.140
Yukina...

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.570
Damn it.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:26.630
You seem to be having some
kind of misunderstanding,

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.830
but Kisa and I are totally lovey-dovey.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:30.640
What?!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.420
He comes and picks me
up from work every day,

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:34.960
so please get it already.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.210
I think things could get
very unpleasant for you...

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:44.930
...if you don't drop this, so maybe
you should just walk away?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.050
What did you say?

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:47.220
What I'm saying is:

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.350
Stay away from him.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.030
Now then...

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.360
Are you hurt?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.000
I'm fine.

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.880
I'm sorry for getting involved.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.240
It's okay. I mean, well...

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.250
Want to go somewhere else?

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:14.710
It's a little crowded here.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.250
Yeah...

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.850
God, I want to die.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.760
I guess that café is closed today.

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:26.640
I live close, so want to come to my place?

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.150
Sorry.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.400
Please excuse that it's a
total single guy's household.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.900
It's totally fine!

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.860
I only have coffee and tea.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.650
Which one would you like?

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.400
I'll have coffee.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:49.660
Oh, yeah, he said he
was an art student...

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.960
Did you ask Yokozawa about these?

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.420
You've got every manga
I ever worked on.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.930
I do?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.550
Is it just a coincidence?

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.860
Maybe I shouldn't have said that.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:16.100
O-Oh, thanks for stepping in back there.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.520
You really saved me.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.390
You even lied for me.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.070
Lied?

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:28.860
You know, when you said
we were going out and such.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.700
Oh, that.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.100
So, uh...

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:38.400
How much did you hear
of all that, anyway?

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:42.450
I stepped in somewhere around
the "Have you done it?"

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.670
O-Oh...

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:46.710
God, no.

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:52.860
I'm sure that's not
anything you know about,

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.910
b-but there are all kinds of
people in the world and...

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:59.120
I suppose you can think of it as
a life experience or something...

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.060
I knew all along.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:06.110
That you kept coming to the store for me.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.270
H-How?!

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.690
I don't want to toot my own horn,

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:15.120
but there are a few customers
who come to the store for me.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:17.830
It was just a feeling.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.370
In the beginning I thought I was
wrong about you since you're a guy.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.280
W-Wrong about...?

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.870
The "here for me" vibe.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.630
Anyway, I noticed you
staring at me a lot.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:32.840
I thought a cute high schooler
took a liking to me,

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:36.640
so when you told me how old you are,
I was really surprised.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.310
I'm sorry.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.970
That's pretty creepy, huh?

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:43.660
I'm sorry, too. For
suddenly kissing you.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:47.570
I want to sink into the ground...

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:50.530
Kisa, you know I...

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:53.470
Please, it's fine! I don't care!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.160
Why don't you care?!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.670
I really do care!

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.250
After that, you just took off!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.710
You stopped coming to the store,

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.170
and you didn't respond to my email.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.260
Well, that's because...

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.970
You were disgusted,
because I'd kissed you?

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.280
After being stared at every day,

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.180
I couldn't help but think about you!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.310
I...

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:19.710
And then,

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:22.600
when I realized you'd been involved with...

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.440
...all of my favorite books, it only got worse.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.460
Uh...

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:32.250
I never knew before that you had
worked on all those books over there.

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.410
They're my favorites.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.080
Th-Thank you.

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:40.450
When stuff like this happens,

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:43.990
can I help but think that it's
fate, like in shojo manga?

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:44.750
Huh?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.440
So then what am I
supposed to do when you say...

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:49.970
...you don't care about me?

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:54.720
I'm sorry, but I'm not quite
sure what you're trying to say.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.570
What I'm saying...

00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.100
...is that I love you.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.610
Well, thank you.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:13.470
I'm very glad if you say
that you love my work....

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.740
But that's not what I'm saying.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.750
I was thinking that I
could do it...with you.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.870
What?!

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:28.630
Will you go out with me?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.050
I...well...

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.020
I'm sorry.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.560
I can't.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.310
Why not?

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:44.950
You heard it before.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:49.320
I don't really know how to love people.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.200
That's why my relationships
never work out.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:57.680
To be perfectly honest,
I was attracted to your face,

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:00.340
but I don't really know
anything about you.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:04.600
I don't know much about you either.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:10.030
You're someone who was on my mind.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.400
Then I realized you'd worked
on all my favorite books,

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.950
and that made me think about you more.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.590
Then I just realized that it's love.

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:21.580
I think this is pretty normal though.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:26.100
Well, it's the first time that
I fell in love with a guy.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:29.190
But I'm fine with it.

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.940
If you like me, too,

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.990
then I'm glad I was born with this face.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:36.470
Damn.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.550
My heart.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:40.740
I really...

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:42.310
...can't.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.320
Kisa!

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:47.500
Kisa, you love me, don't you?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.830
See, I was trying to...

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:53.880
If you do, then why do you run
away as soon as I come towards you?!

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.990
I-I'm very sorry.

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.440
This is probably...

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.420
...because I don't want you to hate me.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.620
Why?

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.980
What do you mean, "why?"

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:13.440
You say you love my books and...

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:19.000
I think you have a really... nice face.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.380
Kisa, have you noticed,

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.870
that even though you keep
saying that you only like my face,

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.600
you haven't looked at my face once?

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.190
And your face is red.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.490
And you're super nervous.

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:34.540
Yeah, because...

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:37.940
That's because you're not just
looking at my face, but all of me.

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:38.800
Right?

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:42.900
I guess I don't really know why it is.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:47.580
My heart's never felt like this before.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:59.450
Isn't that because you
actually really like me?

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:04.580
You know, it's your fault
I kissed you in the café.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:08.260
It's fine for me if you're saying...

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:10.580
...that you're uncertain right now.

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:13.090
I don't think anyone could hold back...

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.960
...if someone looked at them that way.

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.310
All I have to do...is make you love me.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:26.720
He's just holding my hand.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:28.400
Kisa.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:32.480
He's just calling my name.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:35.470
My whole body feels paralyzed.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.740
I'm really warm...

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.010
and I feel like I want to run away.

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:43.270
But I want him to touch me more.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.370
Kisa, I love you.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.880
Is this...

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.670
...what love is?

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.730
Good morning!

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:07.010
Good morning.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.770
Your series needs a second printing.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.140
Really?

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.980
I put it on your desk.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.020
Yes!

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:18.710
They were being stingy
again and wanted only 2,000.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:21.170
I tried to tell them to do 5,000,

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.360
but they wouldn't listen.

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:23.910
Five thousand?!

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.790
Two thousand just isn't enough.

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:29.790
That book is really good,
so it'll sell for a long time.

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:32.290
Thank you.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.260
I need to tell the author.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:40.300
I also want to tell Yukina.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:45.410
Sub: Info
Text: Composing
The book you've been promoting
has just had a second printing run.
Thank you for promoting it.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:55.380
from: Kou Yukina
Sub: Really!?
Congratulations!
See, the books I think
are good just sell!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:04.640
from: Kou Yukina
Sub: And
In fact, it's selling because
I'm promoting it.
You should thank me!

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.660
What the hell?

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.440
He certainly is getting full of himself!

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.890
God, this is annoying.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.540
Just send it all in one message!

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:15.020
from: Kou Yukina
Sub: To Kisa
I love you.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:18.690
Idiot!

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.800
Are you stupid?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:25.510
I don't know anything about Yukina.

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:30.560
Ever since I met him,
my heart's been racing.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.940
I'm thirty, what the hell am I doing?

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.550
I guess this is what they call...

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.290
...first love.

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:58.920
kimi o suki dakeja monotarinai

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:58.920
Simply liking you won't satisfy me

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:04.300
akogare dake ja ume kirenai

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:04.300
Simply admiring you won't satiate me

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:12.390
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:12.390
I fell in love with you

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:15.890
yuugure no kaze no nioi

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:15.890
In a sunset, filled with the scent of the wind

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:20.820
boku wa omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:20.820
When I remember your voice and your smile

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:25.740
kimi no koe sono waraikata

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:25.740
I'm instantly happy

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:30.030
boku wa kimi o suki ni natta

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:30.030
I fell in love with you

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:33.950
dare ni mo mada ietenai

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:33.950
But I haven't been able to tell anyone yet

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:38.420
hitori omoidashite ureshiku naru

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:38.420
When I remember your voice and the way you talk

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.920
sono koe shaberi kata

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.920
Even though I'm alone I'll be happy

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:48.090
samishii kimochi potsuri

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:48.090
The feeling of loneliness... isolated

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:51.510
sukina kimochi kirari

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:51.510
The feeling of love... sparkling

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:57.020
futatsu kubetsu ga tsukanai boku wa

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:57.020
I'm unable to tell these two feelings apart

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:01.650
yuugure ni kokoro tsuburete ku

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:01.650
My heart is slowly crushed as the sun sets

